! Owed at the next #/state true-up (Lares-Awakens seat, 2026-11-07)
* DROP #/state "Rulings the crew still asks of the operator": iframe thread ruled ("Mu on the thread menu", dreamdom.mem:557, 2026-10-29); goldens family + `core` charter ruled 2026-10-20 (dreamdom#/open-rulings, verified); key grain = "standing open, blocks nothing, D1 measures" (measure decides). MOVE household domain + DNS-01 credentials onto the pre-rite's hand list (operator supplies; a hand task, not a ruling). Source: Kiaʻi reading, collided against canon by Awakens.
* ADD the lease-end ruling (lease retires; epoch-roll loss accepted) to the road's #/rulings ONLY after the Luna 2-wave + lease-end census collide it.
* ADD pentabarf V + the talk-out law (operator 2026-11-07) to the road's #/rulings.
* b5b: a Codex reader follows the Opus seam lead's cure (Kiaʻi lean, accepted), before the Luna + blind Opus reads.
* TOOLS FAULT (2026-11-07): tools/seat-walls.mjs runTestSeat vitest argv puts files after `--`; vitest's cac moves them to options['&#45;-'] → whole package runs. Cure: drop the `--` for the vitest runner (the guard already refuses names starting with `-`), red-first in the seat-walls/commit-relay tests (a named file runs ALONE: Test Files 1). Restart every broker after it lands. A free slot takes it (lane `door-filter`) once clock-sweep lands; it passes the focus test (each door call ran a whole package for minutes, and daemon suites broke the single-file law).
* TOOLS FAULT (2026-11-07): launch-codex's pool preflight reads ONLY the newest rollout; a seat launched seconds earlier (no rate_limits record yet) refuses every other launch ("pool line unreadable"). Cure: walk back to the newest rollout that carries a rate_limits record. Hand read at the time: 35% used.
* clock-sweep land read (controller scan, 2026-11-07): the diff mostly REMOVES clocks. One widening to weigh: device-admit's fleet-join daemon-doc wait went 5 s -> DOCUMENT_HANG_BOUND_MS (60 s, find-or-throw.ts:22, "equals the island kernel's hard cap on a slot resolve"); it reads as a named hang bound, not a test greening; weigh it with Luna's verdict. ON_ROLLED_BUDGET_MS cured here moves l27 item 6 out of l27.
* CANON-COLLIDE (Kiaʻi reserve, 2026-11-07; leans at ~/.lares-scratch/canon-collide/reserve-leans.md; Awakens spot-checked items 1+2: they reproduce):
** GRAMMAR LANE (a free slot; its bundle gap folds into the pre-rite's one labelled re-bake): sigil-aka.tid:6 `observe` and sigil-kahea.tid:8 `dataflow` -> `transclusion` per the 2026-10-03 ruling (56856ec82; aka.mem:27,51); align meme-ast/builder.ts:218,229; grep consumers first; no alias.
** CANON TRUE-UP (canon lane at the next batch land): burn the five "Source of truth for X in path" sentences + copied regexes (aka.mem:134 and kin); re-true federated-causal-islands (#/edge-island-shape, #/sync-order, #/lifecycle, #/relay-law) to the live gate BEFORE any M8 lane; Orichalcum bound to the Keyhive read|admin cap, ladder = model vocabulary; no-global-now carrier's oracle-plan sections o-takiage; road :518 cite -> tests/laws/custody-stays-behind-the-door.law.test.ts; L29 row cites `_handleTeardown`, not a line.
* clock-sweep step 25 (apply when step 24 hands back; Kiaʻi lean + controller drift-ward agree): "a line not seen before" fails on lines carrying counters/timestamps/pids ("retry 41", "retry 42" renew forever). RULING: renew the boot wait's LIVENESS span only on a named boot-progress MILESTONE that advances a monotone stage (a repeat or regress renews nothing); if the node logs no named stages, add them at the node's real boot phases (an event the node owns). Normalizing digits is a heuristic and stays out. The red's control: a looping node whose lines differ only in a counter ends 'silent'.
* clock-sweep step 26 (apply after step 25 hands back): BLIND OPUS (seats/blind-opus.md) LAND-AFTER-CURES. Controller ruling, talked out: A LOCK ALWAYS DROPS THE SIGNER (security outranks durability). F1 P1: uds-channel.ts:968-972 awaits beforeSignerDrops -> sealedRestLock -> store.flush (sealed-doc-store.ts:192) -> door asker (sealed-rest.ts:148, no clock): an island alive but silent keeps the signer seated after lock. Cure: the seal ask ends on its answer, worker exit, or a named `// LIVENESS:` island-silence bound that REFUSES (as daemon-vm-core's ISLAND_ASK_LIVENESS_MS does); the signer drops after that bound in every case; titles left unsealed report unsaved by name, never rest clear. Red: a docstore door whose island never answers, close the session, signer.drop fires; control: an answering island seals first, then drops. F2 P2: open-browser-daemon-vm.ts:121 detaches the docstore door only on terminate; wire the browser Worker's error/crash to detach the cell (refuse every waiting ask by name). Red + control. F3 P2: portTransit lost its 20 s; nodeWorkerHandle attaches no cas:want answerer for session islands; prove the session-island CAS miss path never runs (a test), or answer cas:want for session islands with a refusal. P3s owed: isValidDocumentId skip (sealed-rest.ts:522).
* SECURITY (blind door read, 2026-11-07; confirmed by the controller: one inode 161959, 8 links, mode 755, shared by the main checkout and every lane worktree's node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs): provision-worktree hardlinks node_modules (pnpm &#45;-offline install + hardlinkTree), so a walled lead with workspace-write over its worktree can write through the links into the main checkout's and every lane's tooling. NEXT FREE SLOT, ahead of the grammar lane: lane `store-wall`: copy-install (package-import-method=copy, or a lane-private store) for lane worktrees, plus read-only binds of node_modules in the test door's bwrap; red: a write through a lane's node_modules file leaves the main checkout's inode unchanged. Measure the disk cost per worktree first (the disk law: stop under 60G). Also verify the shared store's integrity once (no lead wrote through it).
* store-wall also takes: commit-relay.mjs:48 readHeldAsync reads req-*.json without the O_NONBLOCK + regular-file guard (a lead-planted FIFO stalls the broker for good); red: mkfifo req-N.json under &#45;-once refuses by name, never hangs.
* l27 item 6 (2026-11-07): re-measure 'a ward refusal after ON_ROLLED_BUDGET_MS reads pending and names no reason' against clock-sweep's landed awaitOnRolled (boolean, no pending, no clock); if any ward refusal still names no reason, a row.
* road :49 rank-1 row: its 'Kairos for the seat' sentence still describes the Kiaʻi->Awakens pass and 'span stands at e723dda17'; rewrite evergreen to this pass (or burn it if #/state carries the kairos alone) and true the span head (Kiaʻi, 2026-11-07).
W3 RULING (controller + reserve seat Kiaʻi, 2026-11-07; apply to mesh-seat state when step 3 returns). Case (b), measured: the failing tail at 1a88d7ad5 (run 42383507074, job 128436554220) shows only to-worker posts (the control-event, then two port:place) and NO lar:control-result back. The LIVENESS bound stays (it ends a wait that has a terminal event; removing it would hang the weld on a silent worker). END STATE: every refusal on the return leg reaches the page as a lar:control-result carrying its reason, never a console line alone. Code leads (inferred): (1) packages/lararium-browser/src/surface-return-leg.ts:50 answers a control-event naming a surface the vessel does not hold at that beat with "[vessel] surface-unknown" on the console and returns "surface-unknown" (wired at open-browser-vessel.ts:2273-2276), posting NO control-result; page-wait's terminal regex reads only [daemon-island:fault] and [mirror] stand refused:, so it reads as silence. First: grep the failing run's console capture for "[vessel] surface-unknown". (2) For the daemon's surface ("lares") the leg routes to doors.daemon().sendControlEvent(ev) (:59); the header (:11) promises stale-target only on the pool path: check the daemon island answers an unknown or retired render id with its stale control-result in every case, a port:place re-epoch between included. RED: post port:place and the stale control-event back to back with no await (the race forced, never luck); control: a known render id still runs.
* (owed row, browser return leg, BEFORE THE RITE, conditions from the reserve seat accepted 2026-11-07) the W3 end state above. Red: a click on a surface the vessel does not hold (surface-unknown) and on a retired id (stale-target) each reaches the page as a lar:control-result carrying its reason; control: a known id applies. When it lands, W3's console-refusal arm burns IN THE SAME COMMIT (no two arms; no back-compat) and the weld reads the control-result alone. Context: mesh-seat's 0af53c862 reads the worker's named console stale-target refusal; the product still owes a lar:control-result for every return-leg refusal (surface-unknown and stale-target), never a console line alone.
* (owed row, BEFORE THE RITE, beside the return leg; reserve seat 2026-11-07) packages/lararium-web/src/workers/vessel-host.ts:450 refuses a click silently as session-unadmitted and on a vessel light failure: each answers the page with a lar:control-result under its own refusal word; control-event-pending stays silent (an answer would land on the first act's event id).

